# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Atomik Clips — NEW UI, production build (Vercel)
#
# This file is for the DEPLOYED build only. Set these same three values in
# Vercel's Environment Variables UI — Vercel does not read this file from git,
# it is here as the checklist of what must be set.
#
# The local-dev auth bypass (VITE_LOCAL_DEV / VITE_LOCAL_DEV_SIGNED_OUT /
# VITE_LOCAL_DEV_ROLES) is DELIBERATELY ABSENT and must never be added here.
# vite.config.ts already refuses to stub Clerk when mode === "production", so a
# real build cannot ship the bypass — but leaving the flags out entirely means
# nobody has to rely on that guard.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── REQUIRED — the app will not render without this ──
# The real ClerkProvider refuses to mount without a valid publishable key: it is
# not "you can't log in", the whole React tree fails to boot. This is the pk_live_
# (or pk_test_) key from the Clerk dashboard.
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ── REQUIRED — where the API lives ──
# MUST include the /trpc path: this value is passed straight to the tRPC
# httpLink, and without the path every call 404s against the Express root.
# Unset, the app derives the URL from the page's own host, which is correct
# locally (Vite proxies /trpc) and wrong on Vercel, where nothing is proxied.
VITE_TRPC_URL=https://YOUR-BACKEND-HOST/trpc

VITE_ENVIRONMENT=production

# ── Optional ──
# VITE_RUDDERSTACK_WRITE_KEY=
# VITE_RUDDERSTACK_DATA_PLANE_URL=
